#!/usr/bin/env xetal
## A macro library of your own: userlibs/Repeat.xtlm (in the live demo,
## Repeat.xtlm among your files). It is found as a library of your own
## is, and its macro r:t_imes< writes statements as many times as you
## ask, when the program is expanded: a loop unrolled before it runs.
##
## Run it with ./demos/user-macros.xtl or "xetal run
## demos/user-macros.xtl". It prints hip hip three times, hooray, then
## 32. "xetal expand demos/user-macros.xtl" shows the copies.

"r:" u_se< "Repeat"
"3" r:t_imes< "\"hip hip\""
"hooray"

# The copies are ordinary statements, so they can rebind a variable:
# five doublings, unrolled.
## The number the five unrolled statements double, from 1 to 32.
x! := 1
## Five copies of x! := x! * 2, written by r:t_imes<: x! changes, so it is a ! name.
"5" r:t_imes< "x! := x! * 2"
x!
